  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Disengagement Observer Force (UNDOF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United Nations Disengagement Observer Force (UNDOF) was established by United Nations Security Council Resolution 350 on 31 May 1974, to implement Resolution 338 (1973) which called for an immediate ceasefire and implementation of United Nations Security Council Resolution 242. The mandate of UNDOF has been renewed every six months since 1974 (most recently until 30 August 2016). UNTSO (United Nations Truce Supervision Organization) and UNDOF are operating in the zone and continue to supervise the ceasefire. Before the Syrian Civil War, the situation in the Israel-Syria ceasefire line had remained quiet and there had been no serious incidents. Funding under this activity represents Australia&apos;s assessed contribution to the operation.</narrative>
  </description>
